==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]]

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 73.33~80 seconds<sup>2,200f~2,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 93.33~100 seconds<sup>2,800f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 10~166.67 seconds<sup>300f~5,000f</sup>.
*5 [[Li'l Macho Legs Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Macho Legs Cats]] spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*4 [[Li'l Macho Legs Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Macho Legs Cats]] spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Li'l Macho Legs Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Macho Legs Cats]] spawn after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 240 seconds<sup>7,200f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] makes this stage a joke with Attack Up [[Cat Combo]]s. All you have to do is fill the top row with at least one small Attack Combo (assuming he is level 30), and then send out Awakened Bahamut: he will be able to continuously knock back the Li'l Macho Legs before they have a chance to attack. This stage can also be done with all the [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Rangers]], as they gain wave immunity via [[Helmet Cat (Special Cat)|Helmet Cat's]] [[Yellow Strike (Combo)|Yellow Strike Combo]], just add in Awakened Bahamut Cat, or [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]/[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]—preferably Ramen over Courier, though, as Courier dies fairly quickly. Ramen lets you stall efficiently, thus stacking up enough cash to send out many Nyanko Rangers.

